{"surface": "inspector", "title": "Full text", "html": "<header class=\"hero\"><p class=\"kicker\">Full text</p><h2 class=\"title\">benzinga.com</h2><p class=\"ctx\"><a href=\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/11/63452585/trump-nvidia-stock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/11/63452585/trump-nvidia-stock</a> · read Nov 19, 2026</p></header><div class=\"page md\" data-md=\"# Trump Discloses Up to $380,000 in Nvidia Buys, Calls Huang’s Exit ‘Such a Tragedy’\n\nPresident **Donald Trump’s** portfolio bought between \\$152,004 and \\$380,000 in **Nvidia Corp.** [(NASDAQ:NVDA)](https://www.benzinga.com/quote/NVDA) stock in September, according to an ethics disclosure released Thursday.\n\nIt sold up to \\$15,000 on Sept. 24. That evening, Nvidia’s then-CEO **Jensen Huang** sat at the head table as Trump hosted Chinese President **Xi Jinping** at the White House.\n\nMost of the [buying](https://extapps2.oge.gov/201/Presiden.nsf/PAS%2BIndex/20A6220DE9740AF085258EB400334364/$FILE/Donald-J-Trump-11.01.2026-278T%20optimized%20version.pdf) came in two trades on Sept. 2. The Nvidia sale was one of 109 trades the portfolio made on Sept. 24.\n\nThose trades were small next to Trump’s overall Nvidia stake. The Washington Post [estimated](https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2026/11/16/trumps-stake-nvidia-grew-much-62-million-before-scandal-broke-out/) he held \\$13 million to \\$62 million in Nvidia at the end of August.\n\nThe White House said in October that outside firms manage the portfolio and track broad market indexes. It did not immediately respond to a request for comment from Reuters on Thursday.\n\n### What Trump Said About Huang\n\nBy the time Trump and Xi dined again this week in Shenzhen, **Jensen Huang** had stepped down. Trump told Fox News he might have briefly mentioned Huang’s departure to Xi. He called it &quot;such a tragedy.&quot;\n\nHuang resigned Nov. 12 after reports of an affair with Alice Huang (no relation), the former CEO of Megaspeed. U.S. officials suspect she has ties to Chinese intelligence, The New York Times reported.\n\nTrump said Monday he was open to Jensen Huang returning as CEO. Huang said Tuesday he’d come back if the board wanted him, but Nvidia’s directors said they had no plans to [reinstate](https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/11/63374089/nvidia-board-rules-out-jensen-huang-return-despite-calls-for-ceo-comeback) him.\n\nOn Thursday, [Polymarket](https://polymarket.com/event/jensen-huang-rejoins-nvidia-byptptpt/will-jensen-huang-rejoin-nvidia-by-december-31-2026) traders gave Jensen Huang a 5% chance of rejoining Nvidia by year-end. About \\$3.28 million had traded on that deadline. A board seat or formal advisory role would also count.\n\n### China’s Access to Nvidia Chips\n\nThree House committees will [question](https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/11/63408059/altman-huang-comeback) Jensen Huang behind closed doors on Dec. 1 about how Chinese companies gained access to advanced Nvidia chips.\n\nOne company under scrutiny is Megaspeed, which Alice Huang used to run. It rents computing power to Chinese customers from data centers in Southeast Asia, the Associated Press [reported](https://apnews.com/article/nvidia-export-controls-chips-china-remote-access-60f868d3bb430b85a8657b27d421096e). U.S. authorities are [investigating](https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/joint-statement-department-commerce-and-department-justice-megaspeed-investigation) the company over possible export violations.\n\nThat’s the kind of remote access Washington tightened rules on Thursday. Some overseas data centers now need a [license](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-19/pdf/2026-23529.pdf) to give Chinese customers access to advanced U.S. chips.\n\nNvidia’s top lawyer, Tim Teter, is due to appear before the same committees the day after Huang.\n\n*Image: Shutterstock*\n\n**Read Also: [China Lost Its ‘Best Friend’ at Nvidia. A Former Intelligence Officer Says the Fallout Is ‘a Catastrophe’ for Beijing](https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/11/63381135/huang-china-nvidia)**\" data-base=\"https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/11/63452585/trump-nvidia-stock\"></div><p class=\"raw\"><a class=\"rawlink\" data-go=\"raw:src:4\">Full details</a></p>", "wide": true}